OL,3,GNEWSAMiner welcomes pension release but
OL,4,Aurges speed
OL,5,
OL,6,FA former miner has welcomed a move to
OL,7,Fend a decades-long battle over pension
OL,8,Fsurplus.
OL,10,FThey say they lost out when a deal was
OL,11,Fstruck in 1994 when British Coal was
OL,12,Fprivatised, meaning while the value of
OL,13,Fthe fund would not decrease, the
OL,14,Fgovernment was allowed to keep half of
OL,15,Fany investment surplus.
OL,17,FHowever, in his budget announcement
OL,18,FChancellor John Healey pledged that the
OL,19,F50-50 agreement would end and all
OL,20,Fsurplus cash would be paid to pension
OL,21,Fholders.
OL,23,APub: 29-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,394,390,260,160,0,100
